y  quick it's pretty fast paced um even  though i guessed like a lot of the stuff  that was gonna happen  it was still pretty entertaining kind of  just going along for the ride  and uh you know the imagery of the witch  was actually really creepy and some of  the weird [ __ ] that happened to them in  the woods like i really liked  the build up and like the imagery and  [ __ ] like that was like really eerie i  liked that um there was just enough  ambiguity to kind of like keep it  interesting and like keep me reading  even though i had figured some stuff out  ahead of time as i said i kind of wish  that hank's you know unreliable narrator  status wasn't so  glaringly obvious like from pretty much  the beginning of the story  but um as i said the story did actually  manage to surprise me a couple times i  wasn't sure exactly where it was going  even though i kind of got in the  ballpark um but yeah so if you like  things like the ritual or the blair  witch project and don't really expect  anything that's kind of like too  out there or like too outside of the  bounds of like some horror tropes that  you will probably recognize then it's a  pretty solid read if you like witches  and lost in the woods type stories and  stuff like that so you know if you've  read it or if it sounds interesting to  you then let me know in the comments and  that will do it for this tomes of terror  i will see you guys on the next one bye

